Subject: [PATCH] Restore whole original VM and Wii32 data/address ABI

Upstream-base: 0f5a757947b8778b680d4d1ae7e6df1792a514f2
Prepared-preimage: reviewed complete dc238202203 source prefix

Default whole InterpreterCore/Operations retain all original algorithms and
32-bit numeric/float/frame/opcode semantics. Serialized pointer fields keep
the original72-byte header and12-byte function stride, resolving actual
SDK cached address words rather than widening numeric slots. Native byte
preparation observes real completed NL ownership/domains; source relocation
and caller ownership remain literal, including retail quirks.
Only actual pointer producers/consumers and unaligned scalar reads cross
the native ABI. Historical InterpreterNative/runtime ownership is explicit
DIAGNOSTIC_INTERPRETER only, never linked into the whole-source module.
Original AsyncLoading string consumer uses the same actual cached-word
transport. Game services/main/loading completion are not substituted.

